  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically the proportion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. The individual does not mention or consider the proportion of probability assigned to losses. Instead, the individual focuses on the magnitude of the loss in B and the chance of avoiding a loss (i.e., getting zero) in B versus A. The individual does not evaluate whether one lottery has a greater portion of probability on unfavorable outcomes. Therefore, the information considered by the individual does not match the information required by the decision reason. Furthermore, the individual's justification (focusing on the chance of no loss and the severity of loss) is inconsistent with the rule of preferring the more right-skewed lottery. Since the individual does not reference skewness or the probability distribution of losses, the decision reason was not used. The reasoning is based on a different criterion (avoiding loss vs. loss severity), not on skewness. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

